4.4 Global app states
Every network-backed page must have defined states:
- Initial load: restrained skeletons aligned to final layout; never a spinner-only blank page.
- Partial success: render data that genuinely loaded and mark unavailable sections individually.
- Empty: explain what is missing and offer one relevant next step.
- Error: identify the affected source/action, preserve previous valid data when safe, offer retry, and do not show stale values as fresh.
- Offline/no network: local farm/crop/analysis records remain accessible; online-only sources state unavailable or cached with timestamps.
- Unsaved changes: clear save/cancel/leave-without-saving behaviour.
- Background/local analysis running: show phase, progress and cancellation only if the operation can actually be cancelled.
- Success: confirm the persisted operation, not just the button click.
