Implementation-time verification checklist for external references
Before coding a connector or UI map pattern, open its official documentation and verify the endpoint, access policy, licence, current availability, supported versions and examples. The sources above are guidance and current research references, not permission to ignore changing provider rules. If an endpoint is paused, deprecated or key-gated, choose and document a working supported alternative before showing a live metric.
What “inspired by” means here
- From Linear: consistent chrome, reduced noise and predictable toolbar locations.
- From operational agritech products: farm/field objects, map layers, work history and crop-linked summaries.
