B. What completion means
“Done” means every requirement maps to a real screen or an explicit unavailable state, a component/interaction, a data model/service/calculation, defined success and failure behaviour, provenance/limitations, and a reproducible test. A polished screenshot is not proof that the app works. A named API is not proof that a connector is implemented. There is no honest way to guarantee that no future bug will ever be found; the goal is a traceable release with no knowingly unresolved high-priority requirement and no fake or unsupported success claims.

