10. High-risk cross-page invariants
The following values must never be calculated differently by separate components:
- overall farm status and field status;
- active crop and crop lifecycle state;
- current/latest rotation plan and historical recommendation;
- planned versus actual dates;
- confidence vs Data Coverage;
- source freshness and observation timestamp;
- selected farm/field ID across route transitions;
- water balance, crop suitability and rotation score;
- alert state and report state;
- Simple/Advanced mode visibility.
If the page header says Good while a water section says critical, the implementation is wrong. If Weather shows a new farm while Soil shows the old farm, implementation is wrong. If an AI explanation disagrees with the deterministic score calculation, the explanation layer must be corrected or marked invalid. If a new run changes an old report, historical immutability is broken.
11. Test design and release gates
Use unit, integration, browser end-to-end and visual regression checks. The release gate is a requirements traceability matrix that ties each prompt requirement to code location/test/evidence, not simply “the app builds”.
11.1 Domain unit tests
- geometry validation/area/unit conversion;
- duplicate farm name normalization;
- crop lifecycle transitions and invalid transition rejection;
- field-area vs farm-boundary tolerance;
- water-balance calculation with known fixture values, unit conversions and missing input;
- weighted score normalization, all-zero weights, infeasible candidates and close-score treatment;
- crop suitability and critical constraints;
- duration windows, leap years/date boundaries, perennial crops and unknown planting dates;
- model confidence and coverage calculations with missing/stale/incompatible sources;
- status priority and unknown-state handling;
- alert deduplication, acknowledgement vs resolution;
- scenario isolation and immutable baseline snapshot.
11.2 Adapter/integration tests
- valid and invalid provider responses;
- no API key, bad API key, rate limit, timeout, server 5xx, malformed JSON, missing values, conflicting sources and partial success;
- provider changes variable names/schema;
- different timezone/day boundary;
- cache hit, expired cache and stale result;
- imagery has clouds/no-data/no valid pixels;
- satellite pipeline unavailable must show unavailable, not synthetic NDVI;
- Gemini disabled/unavailable with deterministic explanation fallback;
- API key never appears in bundle, local export, logs or AI prompts.
11.3 End-to-end workflows
1. Fresh installation -> no fake farms -> run New Analysis in valid location -> review trade-off questions -> select/save result -> Save as Plan -> Calendar reflects plan.
