FIELD SHIFT — SIMPLE MODE vs. ADVANCED MODE: FULL DATA CONTENT SPECIFICATION
What data appears on every page, in each mode. No visual, layout, or styling guidance — content only.
To the AI building this: Simple Mode and Advanced Mode are not two different features or two different calculations — they are two different views into the exact same underlying FarmAnalysis data. Simple Mode shows a curated, plain-language subset; Advanced Mode shows everything, including every raw number, breakdown, and technical methodology. The engine always computes the full Advanced-level data regardless of which mode the farmer is in — the mode only controls what's revealed. This is a single global toggle (set once, applies everywhere) — a farmer should never be in Simple Mode on one page and Advanced on another unless they deliberately drill into something. Below is the complete content list for every page, split by mode.
0. GLOBAL RULE FOR EVERY PAGE
Simple Mode shows:
The single most important conclusion or status first.
Plain-language sentences instead of raw scores wherever a raw score would need explaining.
At most 2–3 supporting facts beneath the headline — enough to trust the conclusion, not enough to require study.
A way to reach more detail (e.g., "See more") rather than hiding it entirely — Simple Mode narrows, it doesn't wall off.
Advanced Mode adds, on top of everything Simple Mode shows (never instead of):
Every raw numeric score and sub-score.
Every component breakdown (the individual factors that produced a composite number).
Provenance/data-source tags on every value.
Confidence breakdowns (not just the High/Moderate/Limited label, but what produced it).
Uncertainty ranges (percentile bands, rank-stability percentages).
The full scientific/technical explanation alongside the plain-language one.
Historical trajectories and multi-season data series, not just end states.
Methodology references (which formula, which dataset, which threshold was used).
1. GLOBAL HEADER / CROSS-PAGE ELEMENTS
   Simple Mode:
   Active farm name + location.
   Alerts bell: shows a count and, on open, each alert's plain-language message only.
   Settings: units (metric/imperial), Simple/Advanced toggle itself, basic notification preferences.
   Advanced Mode adds:
   Alerts bell detail view: the full alert record (observed value, historical baseline, anomaly delta, which satellite/source detected it).
   Settings: data-source preferences, cache/refresh status, engine/crop-database version numbers, export options.
2. HOME PAGE
   Simple Mode:
   Current weather snapshot (temperature, rain/no rain, simple comparison to normal).
   Current crop in the ground, which stage of the rotation, days until the next change.
   One-line rotation sequence with the active crop highlighted.
   One plain sentence each for water status and soil status.
   One suggested next action, or "nothing needed right now."
   Active alerts, if any, in plain language only.
   Advanced Mode adds:
   Full atmospheric detail: wind speed/direction, humidity percentage, solar radiation (insolation), 24-hour rainfall total in mm.
   Soil moisture broken out by depth (topsoil vs. root zone), as a percentage, not just a status word.
   Disease-risk score (not just present on the Rotations page — surfaced here too if the engine computes a live value) with the humidity/wet-canopy hours that produced it.
   Nitrogen balance in kg N/ha remaining in the topsoil, not just a soil-health sentence.
   Days-until-review countdown with the reasoning for that countdown.
   Any detected trend note (e.g., "soil moisture below normal for 2 weeks") shown with its actual duration and magnitude, not just the flag.
