   3–4 plain "why this works" bullets (e.g., "Breaks pest and disease cycles," "Adds nitrogen back to the soil," "Uses less water than your current approach," "Fits your local climate").
   Simple impact summary, in everyday terms: expected yield change, soil-health direction, water-use direction, resilience direction — described as "more/less/about the same," not raw percentages, unless the farmer taps to see the number.
   Botanical family tag per crop, named simply (e.g., "Legume," "Grain," "Oilseed") without requiring scientific naming, with a one-line note on why family matters ("different families break pest cycles for each other").
