   Uncertainty data: the score's percentile range (low-end/high-end estimate), and the percentage of simulated scenarios in which this rotation actually comes out on top.
   Full crop-period breakdown: explicit calendar date window, crop stage, planting/harvest windows and the estimated/confirmed number of days the crop is in the field. Use Year only as an outer multi-year grouping; do not replace date windows with a generic season/year label.
   Water demand vs. supply detail: the crop's water need in mm compared against the expected rainfall/irrigation envelope for that window, and the number of water-stress days expected per season.
   Soil nitrogen contribution, exact figures: kg N/ha added or consumed by each crop, and how that nitrogen credit decays across the following seasons.
   Soil organic matter trajectory: the expected percentage across each season of the cycle, not just a single end-state sentence.
   Disease & pest interruption detail: which specific soil-borne pathogens or pests are being broken by this sequence (named, e.g., a specific fungal pathogen or nematode type relevant to the crop families involved), and how long a break this rotation provides.
   Full crop suitability factor breakdown per crop: temperature/season fit, water fit, soil pH fit, drainage fit, salinity fit, slope fit, growing-period fit — each as its own figure, plus which one (if any) is the limiting factor.
   Rejection detail per rejected rotation: the exact factor that failed, the actual computed value, the safety threshold it exceeded, and by how much — individually, not just the grouped summary.
