   Per-crop duration reasoning: for any multi-season crop, why it stays for the number of seasons chosen and not longer or shorter.
   Review-date reasoning: why the reassessment point was set where it was.
   Order-dependence explanation: why this specific crop order (not just this crop set) was chosen — what carries over from one step to the next.
   Data source/provenance tag on every number above — which came from satellite data, which from the farmer, which are calculated, which are estimated.
   The full technical/scientific explanation text, separate from and in addition to the plain-language explanation.
