32. Final product definition
Home is the concise status entry point. Maps is the geographic workspace with private own-farm outlines and a separate city-level public health layer. Farm Analysis is the structured tracking dashboard that distinguishes the recommended rotation from an actual plan, displays all relevant available measurements and derived indicators with honest provenance, logs farming activity and outcomes, and links to detailed investigations. Deep Analysis remains an existing button and system with its own dated-log secondary page and closeable detailed log popup. Calendar remains a separate main-navigation page. Rotation remains linked to the existing Rotations page.

The most important rule across every page is to distinguish what was measured, what was retrieved, what was predicted, what was calculated, what was reported by the farmer, and what is unknown. A polished interface must not imply precision that the data does not provide. Build around the current code and data integrations, validate each calculation, and phase in new trackers according to evidence availability and agricultural relevance.
