Mandatory dispositions for known legacy risks
- Remove seeded farms/accounts falsely presented as verified or real.
- Remove any simulated NDVI/vegetation data generated from rainfall thresholds or fixed constants. NDVI requires actual compatible red/NIR reflectance or a real validated provider product.
- Remove fabricated fallback locations, soil properties, annual precipitation, crop history, moisture percentiles, and default rotation context from AI prompts.
- Remove hard-coded confidence claims and hidden ideal values for missing soil/water measurements. Missing evidence must remain missing or be represented as a documented estimate with source/uncertainty.
- Remove silent rewriting of crop history into Fallow/Cover Crop; use explicit user-confirmed lifecycle events.
- Merge duplicate navigation implementations; establish one authoritative route and selected farm/field state.
- Remove seeded/demo authentication and account identity in the current no-login build.
- Replace multi-theme and globally filtered map tiles with one dark-only forest agricultural intelligence visual system; never globally colour-filter satellite imagery.
- Keep all API keys out of browser code. Where the deployment cannot provide a server proxy/key, show provider as unconfigured/unavailable rather than exposing secrets.
- Preserve working agronomic calculations only after auditing assumptions, units, source quality, missing-data behavior and test coverage.
