Tile sizes may vary by context, but use the hierarchy: 16–18 px line icon at top-left; metric label immediately below or to its right in 12–13 px muted text; value 24–30 px semibold, with unit baseline-aligned at 12–14 px; optional status/change on a third line with icon and descriptive word. Use tabular numbers. Do not show percentages as 0–100 without defining the denominator. A missing value shows an em dash only with a Not available tooltip or explicit state, never 0. A tile opens relevant detail only if it can provide a meaningful drill-down.
