97. Sign-off: when a frontend component is truly finished
A component is not complete just because its first render looks attractive. It is complete only when:
- its placement and hierarchy match this contract;
- its typography, units, colour, icon and image treatment are intentional;
- content comes from the correct selected farm/field and current saved state;
- Simple Mode and Advanced Mode differ exactly in information depth, not results;
- every action works and its persistence/undo/delete consequence is clear;
- empty, partial, stale, error and unavailable states are designed;
- its relevant evidence/source/uncertainty is accessible;
- keyboard, touch, responsive, reduced-motion and accessibility checks pass;
- the visual composition stays legible with long names, missing data and narrow viewport;
- its implementation is covered by a test and screenshots in the QA report.
If any item is not met, the component remains “in progress”. No route may be marked complete based only on a desktop screenshot of its happy path.with others. 